 "titulo": "Why old wooden bridges had roofs 🇨🇭 #engineering #shorts",
 "capa": "THE ROOF IS FOR THE BRIDGE",
 "descripcion": "Covered bridges weren't built to keep travelers dry. The roof protects the wooden beams from rain, and turns a 20-year bridge into a 100-year bridge. Lucerne's Chapel Bridge dates from 1333.\n\nWhat should we explain next?\n\n#howitworks #engineering #science #shorts",
